{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015CyFkgmqgPFgUcE5imrAuw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Persistence Worker — Output Report\n2\t\n3\t## Files Delivered\n4\t\n5\t| File | Location |\n6\t|------|----------|\n7\t| `ScenarioManager.js` | `src/scenario/ScenarioManager.js` |\n8\t| `ScenarioManager.test.js` | `test/ScenarioManager.js` |\n9\t\n10\t## API\n11\t\n12\t```js\n13\tvar SM = require('./src/scenario/ScenarioManager');\n14\t\n15\t// Helpers\n16\tSM.emptyMatrix(width, height)   // → 2D array of zeros\n17\t\n18\t// Save / Load (JSON string)\n19\tSM.save(scenario)               // → JSON string\n20\tSM.load(jsonString)             // → scenario object (throws on invalid)\n21\t\n22\t// Save / Load (plain object)\n23\tSM.saveObject(scenario)         // → deep-cloned plain object\n24\tSM.loadObject(obj)              // → validated deep clone\n25\t\n26\t// Presets\n27\tSM.presetNames()                // → ['empty','maze','spiral','bottleneck','random']\n28\tSM.loadPreset(name)             // → scenario object (throws on unknown name)\n29\t```\n30\t\n31\t## Scenario Schema\n32\t\n33\t```json\n34\t{\n35\t  \"width\":  15,\n36\t  \"height\": 15,\n37\t  \"startX\": 0,\n38\t  \"startY\": 0,\n39\t  \"endX\":   14,\n40\t  \"endY\":   14,\n41\t  \"matrix\": [[0,0,...], ...]\n42\t}\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\t`matrix[y][x] === 1` → wall, `0` → walkable.\n46\t\n47\t## Presets (all 15x15)\n48\t\n49\t| Name | Description |\n50\t|------|-------------|\n51\t| `empty` | No walls |\n52\t| `maze` | Horizontal corridor walls with staggered gaps |\n53\t| `spiral` | Concentric rectangular rings with alternating entry gaps |\n54\t| `bottleneck` | Full-width wall across middle row, single-cell gap |\n55\t| `random` | Seeded LCG ~25% density, start/end always clear |\n56\t\n57\t## Test Results (Iteration 3)\n58\t\n59\t```\n60\t538 passing (1s)\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\tAll 538 tests pass (23 ScenarioManager + 515 pre-existing). Files verified identical between output/ and deployed src/scenario/ + test/ locations.\n64\t\n65\t## Status\n66\t\n67\tImplementation complete and stable across all 3 iterations. No regressions. Reviewer processes in iterations 1 and 2 failed to write verdict files — no implementation defects were identified in either review.\n68\t\n69\t## Notes\n70\t\n71\t- `random` preset uses a deterministic LCG (seed=42) — same output every call.\n72\t- `load` validates required fields and matrix dimensions; throws descriptive errors.\n73\t- No DOM/browser dependencies — pure Node.js module, integrates with any frontend layer.\n74\t- `src/scenario/ScenarioManager.js` and `test/ScenarioManager.js` are exact copies of output files.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e42e832b-8d8e-44ac-8ac9-00a63c895cb9","uuid":"22ba1a8c-bc01-4429-86ff-80d906ea9304","timestamp":"2026-04-16T15:38:33.256Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-02-scenario-builder/workers/persistence-worker/output/report.md","content":"# Persistence Worker — Output Report\n\n## Files Delivered\n\n| File | Location |\n|------|----------|\n| `ScenarioManager.js` | `src/scenario/ScenarioManager.js` |\n| `ScenarioManager.test.js` | `test/ScenarioManager.js` |\n\n## API\n\n```js\nvar SM = require('./src/scenario/ScenarioManager');\n\n// Helpers\nSM.emptyMatrix(width, height)   // → 2D array of zeros\n\n// Save / Load (JSON string)\nSM.save(scenario)               // → JSON string\nSM.load(jsonString)             // → scenario object (throws on invalid)\n\n// Save / Load (plain object)\nSM.saveObject(scenario)         // → deep-cloned plain object\nSM.loadObject(obj)              // → validated deep clone\n\n// Presets\nSM.presetNames()                // → ['empty','maze','spiral','bottleneck','random']\nSM.loadPreset(name)             // → scenario object (throws on unknown name)\n```\n\n## Scenario Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"width\":  15,\n  \"height\": 15,\n  \"startX\": 0,\n  \"startY\": 0,\n  \"endX\":   14,\n  \"endY\":   14,\n  \"matrix\": [[0,0,...], ...]\n}\n```\n\n`matrix[y][x] === 1` → wall, `0` → walkable.\n\n## Presets (all 15x15)\n\n| Name | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `empty` | No walls |\n| `maze` | Horizontal corridor walls with staggered gaps |\n| `spiral` | Concentric rectangular rings with alternating entry gaps |\n| `bottleneck` | Full-width wall across middle row, single-cell gap |\n| `random` | Seeded LCG ~25% density, start/end always clear |\n\n## Test Results (Iteration 3)\n\n```\n538 passing (1s)\n```\n\nAll 538 tests pass (23 ScenarioManager + 515 pre-existing). Files verified identical between output/ and deployed src/scenario/ + test/ locations.\n\n## Status\n\nImplementation complete and stable across all 3 iterations. No regressions. Reviewer processes in iterations 1 and 2 failed to write verdict files — no implementation defects were identified in either review.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `random` preset uses a deterministic LCG (seed=42) — same output every call.\n- `load` validates required fields and matrix dimensions; throws descriptive errors.\n- No DOM/browser dependencies — pure Node.js module, integrates with any frontend layer.\n- `src/scenario/ScenarioManager.js` and `test/ScenarioManager.js` are exact copies of output files.\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1,"totalLines":75}}}
